# **WordPress Block Spacing System**

## **Core Philosophy**

- **No Default Padding**: Groups have zero padding by default to prevent stacking
- **Intentional Spacing**: Only apply padding when explicitly needed for visual containers
- **Flow-Based Rhythm**: Use `gap` and flow patterns for consistent spacing between elements
- **Utility Override**: Provide utilities for fine-grained control when needed

## **Group Padding Strategy**

### ✅ **DO: Use Semantic Classes**
```html
<!-- Visual containers that need padding -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-background">...</div>
<div class="wp-block-group is-style-container">...</div>
<div class="wp-block-group is-style-section">...</div>

<!-- Site structure containers -->
<header class="wp-block-group site-header">...</header>
<main class="wp-block-group site-main">...</main>
<footer class="wp-block-group site-footer">...</footer>
```

### ❌ **DON'T: Apply Universal Padding**
```css
/* AVOID - This creates padding hell */
.wp-block-group {
  padding: var(--wp--preset--spacing--medium);
}
```

## **Spacing Patterns**

### **1. Flow Spacing (Automatic)**
```css
/* Applied automatically to flow layouts */
.wp-block-group.is-layout-flow > * + * {
  margin-top: var(--wp--preset--spacing--medium);
}
```

### **2. Gap Spacing (Flex/Grid)**
```html
<!-- Use gap classes for flex/grid containers -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-gap-small is-layout-flex">...</div>
<div class="wp-block-group has-gap-medium is-layout-grid">...</div>
```

### **3. Section Spacing (Major Layout)**
```html
<!-- For major page sections -->
<section class="wp-block-group has-section-spacing">...</section>
<section class="wp-block-group has-section-spacing-large">...</section>
```

## **Available Utility Classes**

### **Gap Control**
- `has-gap-none` - No gap between flex/grid items
- `has-gap-small` - Small gap (--spacing-small)
- `has-gap-medium` - Medium gap (--spacing-medium)
- `has-gap-large` - Large gap (--spacing-large)
- `has-gap-xl` - Extra large gap (--spacing-xl)

### **Margin Control**
- `has-margin-top-none` - Remove top margin
- `has-margin-top-small` - Small top margin
- `has-margin-top-medium` - Medium top margin
- `has-margin-top-large` - Large top margin
- `has-margin-bottom-none` - Remove bottom margin
- `has-margin-bottom-small` - Small bottom margin
- `has-margin-bottom-medium` - Medium bottom margin
- `has-margin-bottom-large` - Large bottom margin

### **Flow Control**
- `has-no-child-margins` - Remove all child margins
- `has-tight-flow` - Reduce spacing between children
- `has-loose-flow` - Increase spacing between children
- `is-content-flow` - Content-only container (no padding, flow spacing)
- `breaks-flow` - Break vertical rhythm chain

### **Section Spacing**
- `has-section-spacing-small` - Small section padding
- `has-section-spacing` - Standard section padding
- `has-section-spacing-large` - Large section padding

### **Manual Padding (Use Sparingly)**
- `has-padding-small` - Explicit small padding
- `has-padding-medium` - Explicit medium padding  
- `has-padding-large` - Explicit large padding
- `has-no-padding` - Force remove padding

## **Common Patterns**

### **Site Header**
```html
<header class="wp-block-group site-header has-section-spacing-small">
  <div class="wp-block-group has-gap-medium is-layout-flex">
    <div class="wp-block-group site-branding has-gap-small">
      <!-- Logo and title -->
    </div>
    <nav class="wp-block-group has-gap-small">
      <!-- Navigation -->
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
```

### **Content Section**
```html
<section class="wp-block-group has-section-spacing">
  <div class="wp-block-group is-content-flow">
    <!-- Flowing content with automatic vertical rhythm -->
    <h2>Heading</h2>
    <p>Paragraph with automatic spacing</p>
    <div class="wp-block-group has-background">
      <!-- This card gets padding, content inside flows naturally -->
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
```

### **Breaking Flow for Special Cases**
```html
<div class="wp-block-group is-content-flow">
  <h2>Section Title</h2>
  <p>Introduction text</p>
  
  <!-- This image shouldn't have top margin -->
  <figure class="wp-block-image breaks-flow">
    <img src="hero.jpg" alt="Hero image">
  </figure>
  
  <!-- Content after break resumes normal flow -->
  <p class="has-margin-top-medium">Caption text</p>
</div>
```

## **Migration from Old System**

### **Replace Inline Styles**
```html
<!-- OLD -->
<div class="wp-block-group" style="padding-top: var(--wp--preset--spacing--medium)">

<!-- NEW -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-section-spacing-small">
```

### **Replace blockGap Styles**
```html
<!-- OLD -->
<div class="wp-block-group" style="gap: var(--wp--preset--spacing--small)">

<!-- NEW -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-gap-small">
```

### **Nested Group Cleanup**
```html
<!-- OLD - Padding stacks -->
<div class="wp-block-group" style="padding: 1rem;">
  <div class="wp-block-group" style="padding: 1rem;">
    <!-- 2rem total padding! -->
  </div>
</div>

<!-- NEW - Intentional spacing -->
<div class="wp-block-group has-background">
  <div class="wp-block-group is-content-flow">
    <!-- Outer container provides padding, inner manages flow -->
  </div>
</div>
```

## **When to Use Each Approach**

### **Use Flow Spacing When:**
- Content should have natural vertical rhythm
- Elements are stacked vertically in reading order
- You want automatic, consistent spacing

### **Use Gap Spacing When:**
- Elements are laid out with flexbox or grid
- You need consistent spacing between peer elements
- Layout is primarily horizontal or grid-based

### **Use Explicit Padding When:**
- Creating visual containers (cards, sections)
- Establishing clear content boundaries
- Background colors or borders require internal space

### **Use Manual Utilities When:**
- Breaking or adjusting automatic spacing patterns
- Fine-tuning specific spacing relationships
- Overriding defaults for special cases

## **Performance Notes**

- Gap properties are more performant than margins for flex/grid layouts
- Flow spacing reduces layout calculations compared to individual margins
- Utility classes are cached and reusable
- Avoiding deep specificity improves CSS performance

## **Accessibility Considerations**

- Consistent spacing improves reading flow for all users
- Adequate spacing helps users with motor difficulties
- Logical spacing patterns aid screen reader navigation
- Visual rhythm supports users with cognitive differences

**Remember**: The goal is predictable, maintainable spacing that doesn't require constant overrides or calculations. Start with semantic patterns and use utilities only when the defaults don't meet your needs.
